    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152">

                <pb facs="0147" n="135" xml:id="pg135"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.24/205: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-18T00:00:00-04:00">June 18,
                            1942—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>158. Your despatch no. 272, May 28.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d152-f1"/> We note that
                    British Minister’s letter of May 27 to you lists 1 American and 7 British
                    members of Central Supplies Committee and that apparently Iranians are not
                    represented.</p>
                <p>Your telegram 119, April 23<anchor n="23" xml:id="d152-f2"/> proposed a committee
                    composed of American and British Ministers and representatives of Iranian
                    Ministries of Commerce and Finance, with other British representatives acting in
                    an advisory capacity only, and it was on this basis that Department authorized
                    your participation. (See Department’s 106, April 30.)<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d152-f3"/> Department’s suggestion that tires and other American
                    supplies be distributed under supervision of Central Supplies Committee was made
                    on understanding that Committee would be a joint Anglo-American-Iranian body. If
                    this is not the case, we may have to reconsider our attitude.</p>
                <p>Please telegraph exact composition of committee as now functioning and whether
                    any changes are contemplated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
